      "id": 1,
      "text": "Genola was platted in 1908 as a station on the Soo Line Railroad, then renamed in 1915 from New Pierz to Genola.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genola%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s name comes from Genola, Italy, reflecting the heritage of early settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genola%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Genola’s eastern edge borders the Skunk River, which eventually joins the Mississippi River south of Royalton.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
